                },
                {
                    titleKey: 'round5_title',
                    title: 'Round 5: The Hallucinating AI',
                    description: '<b>Situation:</b> You are preparing for the quarterly business review with the CEO and CFO. You asked Nativa AI to draft the market analysis section including competitive benchmarking and market share data.<br><br><b>Your task:</b> Review the AI output for your executive presentation. This is the most ethically consequential round — how you handle AI-generated content for high-stakes presentations defines your professional integrity.<br><br><b>Key principle:</b> AI use does not transfer accountability. You remain responsible for everything you present.',
                    aiOutput: '<b>Market Analysis - Nativa Fresh Q4 2025 Review</b><br><br>The Colombian dairy alternatives market grew 12.3% YoY (Euromonitor, 2025), outpacing the broader LATAM average of 8.7%. Nativa Fresh maintained category leadership with an estimated 28% value share.<br><br>Key competitive dynamics:<br>- Premium segment growth accelerated to 18.5% YoY (Nielsen Colombia LATAM Consumer Goods Report Q4 2025)<br>- Private label penetration reached 15.2% of value sales (Kantar Worldpanel Colombia, 2025)<br>- Plant-based protein alternatives grew 22% in volume (Mintel LATAM, 2025)<br>- Consumer willingness-to-pay premium index rose from 1.12 to 1.24 (internal Nativa research, 2024)<br><br>Competitive positioning remains strong, with Nativa Fresh scoring highest on brand trust (87/100) and product innovation (82/100) among Colombian consumers aged 25-45.',
                    flawDescription: 'The "Nielsen Colombia LATAM Consumer Goods Report Q4 2025" does not exist — it is a hallucinated citation. Additionally, the Kantar figure (15.2%) is directionally correct but uses 2024 data presented as 2025, making the magnitude outdated.',
                    flawOptions: ["A cited Nielsen report does not exist, and a 2024 Kantar figure is dated 2025", "Colombia growing 12.3% while LATAM grows 8.7% is a contradiction in the data", "Plant-protein growth of 22% must be in value, not in volume, so the figure is mislabelled"],
                    flawCorrect: 1,
